      "text": "A bag used by shepherds or by travelers (1 Sam. 17:40; Matt. 10:10; Mark 6:8; Luke 9:3; 10:4; 22:35–36). The bag was usually made of leather and was used for carrying bread and other food. It should not be confused with a money bag, which was called a purse.",
